task: dataflow-auto-accumulator
agent: opus-dataflow
started: 2026-09-10
branch: feature/dataflow-auto-accumulator
worktree: ../okay-wt-daa1
spec: specs/dataflow.md (stage 2's autoBound)

why: `Finish.Auto` decides from one constant — 100 000 accumulators —
  measured on the CHEAPEST accumulator that exists, a Long count, at
  eight partitions. The doc already says a fatter accumulator moves
  the bound DOWN, which is a prediction sitting in a comment with no
  number under it. A default that has never been measured on the
  shape it is most often wrong about is a guess wearing a
  measurement's clothes.

what: the same table again with Wroclaw's own accumulator — the tuple
  tree `((Long, Long), Option[Int])`, six objects per add — beside the
  count, so the two crossovers can be read against each other. Then
  one of two honest outcomes, and the measurement picks which:

    - the crossovers are close, and one constant serves both; or
    - they are far apart, and no constant serves both — in which case
      `autoBound` is documented for what it is and the doc says what
      to do instead, rather than being re-fitted to the average of two
      jobs neither of which is the caller's.

predict: the fat crossover lands well below 100 000, because merging
  a tuple tree allocates on every combine while the hand-off does not
  change. If it lands within a factor of two I will say one constant
  serves both; if it is an order of magnitude lower, a single default
  cannot be right and the entry closes by saying so.
